WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.670
- Okay, I've watched the
first episode of "She-Hulk."

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.540
- [Hulk] Don't lawyer me.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.890
- Two things stuck out to me.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.810
First is just how terrible

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.430
the closing argument was at the end.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.340
- My client was well within his right

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.190
to protect his business interest.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.060
These accidental deaths were
an unfortunate byproduct

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.620
of an ambitious expansion plan.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.330
- Okay, that's just a terrible argument,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.210
both legally and persuasively,
that a bunch of people died

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:28.050
because you were ambitiously
expanding your business.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:28.980
That's not gonna work.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.860
- [Lawyer] Did my client know
lives would be in danger?

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.490
That is debatable and depends
on your definition of knowing.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.430
- It's a terrible argument that
it depends on the definition

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.370
of knowing that other
people are going to die.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.710
That's bad, legally and persuasively.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.660
Just an all around terrible argument

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.493
that just seems like they threw

00:00:46.493 --> 00:00:48.030
a bunch of legal words together.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.530
But at least there was one bright spot.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.760
At the very beginning of the episode

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.800
as they do a slow pull
away from Jennifer Walters,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.900
it's revealed that she has two degrees,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.790
both of which are from UCLA,

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.010
obviously the best law school out there.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:00:59.883
Go Bruins!

